// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 09-identity-origin-extent
// facility: rule.ref.form [Ref-Form-Not-Place]
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.borrow-of-non-place (static)
//
// A bare call result is not a place expression at all (spec/13 §1:
// the place expressions are a name, `*e`, `e.f`, `e[i]` and `reclaim`),
// whatever its type -- so `&make()` is [Ref-Form-Not-Place], for a
// resource-returning `make` exactly as for a plain one. Only a
// *projection* of a call result or aggregate literal (`&make().f`,
// `&P { .a = 1 }.a`) is a place rooted at a temporary, which is
// [Ref-Form-Temporary]'s case (see borrow_of_temporary_projection_
// rejected.cb). An earlier reading of this file had it the other way.

import std;

fn make() : Vec<i32>
{
    Vec::new()
}

fn main()
{
    auto r = &make();
}
